  "raw_label": "appellant_won",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Maltesh Paitl vs Bruhat Bengaluru Mahanagara Palike on 29 January, 2024 Author: Suraj Govindaraj Bench: Suraj Govindaraj -1- Nc: 2024:Khc:3742 Wp No. 23065 of 2023 In The High Court Of Karnataka At Bengaluru Dated This The 29Th Day Of January, 2024 Before The Hon'Ble Mr Justice Suraj Govindaraj Writ Petition No. 23065 Of 2023 (Lb-Bmp) Between: Maltesh Patil, Fan Hospitality Services Pvt Ltd Mr Malatesh Patil Aged About 48 Years, In Provisions Of Fss Act, 2006 Site No.16, Sy No.45, 46, 48 Ground Floor Beml Employees Co Operative Society Channasandra Village, Uttarahalli Hobli, R R Nagar, Bbmp West Bangalore-560098 ...Petitioner (By Sri. Shanthi Bhushan H.,Advocate) And: Digitally signed 1. Bruhat Bengaluru Mahanagara Palike by Shwetha Raghavendra Represented By Chief Commissioner, Bbmp-Rajarajeshwari Nagar, Location: High Sub Division Court of Bangalore-560098 Karnataka 2. Zonal Commissioner Bbmp Rajarajeshwari Nagar Maltesh Paitl vs Bruhat Bengaluru Mahanagara Palike on 29 January, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/70981554/ 1 Sub Division Bangalore-560098 3. Joint Commissioner Bbmp-Rajarajeshwari Nagar, Sub Division Bangalore-560098 4. Senior Health Inspector -2- Nc: 2024:Khc:3742 Wp No. 23065 of 2023 Bbmp-Rajarajeshwari Nagar, Sub Division Bangalore-560098 5. Medical Health Officer Bbmp-Rajarajeshwari Nagar, Sub Division Bangalore-560098 ...Respondents (By Sri. Satyanand B S.,Advocate For R1 To R5; Smt. Saritha Kulkarni., Hcgp For R6) This Writ Petition Is Filed Under Articles 226 & 227 Of The Constitution Of India Praying To Issue Writ Of Certiorari Or Any Other Appropriate Writs Or Directions Quashing The Impugned Notice Dated 07/10/2023 Bearing No.A.Y/Raranv/P.R/183/2023-24 Issued By R4 Vide Annexure-E And Etc. This Writ Petition, Coming On For Further Hearing, This Day, The Court Made The Following: Order 1. The petitioner is before this Court seeking for the following reliefs: a. Issue a writ of certiorari or any other appropriate writs or directions quashing the impugned notice dated 07.10.2023 bearing No. A.Y/RaRaNV/P.R/183/2023-24 issued by Respondent No.4 vide Annexure-E; b. Issue writ of mandamus or any other appropriate writs or directions directing the Respondents herein to consider the Receipt filed by the petitioner herein for the New Trade Licence for the year 2022-23 vide Annexure-D; Maltesh Paitl vs Bruhat Bengaluru Mahanagara Palike on 29 January, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/70981554/ 2 c. Grant such other and further reliefs as this Hon'ble Court may kindly be pleased to grant in the interest of justice and equity. NC: 2024:KHC:3742 d.",
    "facts": "A trade license for the said business having been applied for on 17.12.2022, Respondent No.5 on 7.10.2023 called upon the petitioner to vacate the premises, since the petitioner was using the basement parking as a kitchen. On 13.12.2023, a submission was made that the application filed by the petitioner had been rejected on the ground that in the basement a kitchen was being run. Hence, the counsel for the petitioner submitted that no such kitchen is being run but only certain items were stored and an affidavit of undertaking would be filed by the petitioner that the basement was not be used for any such purpose, such an affidavit came to be filed on 25.10.2023. 4. Subsequently, the application filed by the petitioner allegedly came to be rejected on the grounds that the property is in a residential area. Hence, an amendment was carried out challenging the same, objections were also filed by the respondent. 5. Initially it was contended by the corporation that the road width in front of the property of the petitioner was NC: 2024:KHC:3742 less than 40 feet and as such the no commercial activity could be carried out therein. In that view of the matter the Karnataka State Fire and Emergency Service Department represented by the Director General of Police and Director General of Fire and Emergency Services was brought on record as party respondent, since the BBMP was not in a position to place on record as to under what provision and what permission is required to be obtained. 6. A report came to be filed enclosing notification dated 20.9.1971 by the learned AGA on behalf of the Fire Department. It was categorically stated that there is no permission which is required from the Fire Department except that certain of the guidelines were required to be followed by a restaurant.",
    "arguments": ""
  },
